Root cause:
The bug was caused by the omission of handling huge pages in the memory cgroup (memcg) statistics for the PGLAZYFREE, PGACTIVATE, and PGDEACTIVATE events. The original implementation did not account for the number of pages in a huge page when updating the statistics, leading to incorrect memory reclaim stats for cgroups. The patch corrects this by ensuring that the number of pages in a huge page is properly counted and reported in the relevant functions. Additionally, it uses an irq-unsafe function to update the PGLAZYFREE event since the interrupt is already disabled at that point, which improves the safety and correctness of the operation.
